# bench-per-commit

`logs/` holds the criterion output the changelog quotes. `cargo bench --locked --bench scheduler` ran at
19b484b, cfb873a, 513cb50, da655cf, c4fe22d, 967b616 and e9f73c3, one after another, then at 19b484b a
second time. 407684b was not benched. `logs/progress.txt` has each run's start and end time and the
load average. It was one Apple Silicon Mac with other work running.

    python3 proofs/bench-per-commit/compare.py 19b484b:e9f73c3 19b484b:19b484b_again

prints the change in criterion's point estimate for each bench.

`run.sh` is the loop that made the logs. That run used a copy of each commit's tree under one folder.
This copy makes the trees with `git archive` in a temp dir and writes the new logs to another temp dir,
so `logs/` stays as it is. The whole loop took 27 minutes.
